### Preamble

LarvIDE was created to help university students in Gaza who cannot afford laptops to complete their assignments on Android phones. The source is made available so students can learn from it, run it, and improve it privately. To prevent exploitation and to protect the author's attribution, distribution of modified versions — especially by organisations — requires explicit permission.

---

### 1. Definitions

1.1  **"Software"** means the LarvIDE source code, documentation, and assets as distributed by the Licensor.
1.2  **"You"** means the individual or Legal Entity exercising permissions under this Licence.
1.3  **"Modify"** means to create a Derivative Work, including editing, translating, or extending the source code.
1.4  **"Private Use"** means use, study, and modification solely for your personal, non-distributed purposes (e.g., fixing a bug for yourself, learning, university assignment).
1.5  **"Distribute"** means to make the Software or a Derivative Work available to any third party, including by publishing to GitHub, distributing an APK/AAB/IPA, uploading to a store, or sharing within an organisation beyond the individual.

### 2. Grant of Rights — Use and Private Modification

Subject to the terms below, the Licensor grants You a **worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive** right to:

a) **Use, run, and study** the Software for any purpose, including educational and non-commercial use by students and universities;
b) **Privately Modify** the Software for your own study and internal, non-distributed use — without needing permission.

No other rights are granted.

### 3. Distribution — What Requires Permission

**3.1  Unmodified Copies:** You may Distribute *verbatim, unmodified* copies of the Software provided You retain all copyright, licence, `NOTICE` and attribution notices, and include a copy of this Licence. You must not misrepresent the origin of the Software. For clarity, "unmodified" includes — and you must not remove or alter — the in-app **About screen** and any copyright, attribution, or branding notices displayed to the end user.

**3.2  Modified Versions — Permission Required:** You may **not** Distribute any modified version or Derivative Work of the Software without **prior explicit written permission** from the Licensor.

This applies to *all* distributors, including but not limited to:

* Companies and commercial entities
* Universities, schools, institutes, and student organisations
* Any group publishing a fork, clone, or re-branded build

Permission requests must be sent to **abdalahalhabbash@gmail.com** with a description of the intended modification and distribution. Permission is granted at the sole discretion of the Licensor and may include conditions (e.g., distinct name/branding).

*Private, non-distributed modifications (Section 2b) do not require permission. The restriction triggers only upon Distribution.*

### 4. Conditions for Permitted Distribution

Where permission is granted under 3.1 or 3.2, You must:

a) Retain `Copyright (c) 2026 Abdallah Al-Habbash (HabbashX)` and this Licence in all copies;
b) Cause modified files to carry a prominent notice stating You changed them and the date of change;
c) Not remove or alter any `NOTICE` or attribution files;
d) Clearly identify Your distribution as a *modified version* — e.g., "Based on LarvIDE by HabbashX" — and not as the official LarvIDE.
e) **University / Institutional Attribution:** If You are a University, School, Institute, or educational organisation that *uses* or *distributes* the Software (even unmodified) for classroom, lab, or coursework purposes, You must give conspicuous credit to the original author where end-users can see it — for example in the application's **About screen**, course material, or lab handout — with the text:

> **Project Developed By Abd Allah Al Habbash — github.com/HabbashX**

   You are encouraged (but not required) to make `github.com/HabbashX` a clickable link so students can discover the original project and its author.

