The Android `android.jar` (bootclasspath) is part of the Android SDK and is used only as a compile-time/runtime reference inside the on-device compiler; it is not redistributed as LarvIDE's own code.

Up-to-date versions and a generated machine-readable bill of materials are published in the official repository at `https://github.com/HabbashX/LarvIDE` (see `app/build.gradle` and any `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES` / `licenses` output bundled with the APK).

